# Feature-Sliced Design (FSD 2.1) & UI Performance Rules

When developing in `src/`:

1. **Feature-Sliced Design (FSD 2.1) Layers:**
   - Hierarchy (strictly top-down): `app` -> `widgets` -> `features` -> `entities` -> `shared`.
   - Upper layers import from lower layers. Lower layers NEVER import from upper layers.
   - Slices on the same layer CANNOT import each other directly (use composition in higher layer).
   - Absolute alias paths `@/*` are required. Relative traversal (`../../..`) is banned.

2. **60/120 FPS Compositor & Performance:**
   - Frame budget: `< 16.6ms`.
   - All animations must use GPU-composited properties (`transform`, `opacity`). Never animate `width`, `height`, `top`, `left`, `margin`.
   - Clean up Three.js (`@react-three/fiber`) geometries and materials with `.dispose()` on unmount.

3. **Database & API Boundaries:**
   - Current database runs on **Drizzle ORM** (`src/shared/api/database/schemas/schema.ts`).
   - Never access the database directly from Client Components (`'use client'`). Use Server Components, Server Actions, or API handlers.
